# 26. IMPORTANT TRACKER RULE: DO NOT DUPLICATE TOPICS

A coding agent should ideally store a topic once and attach multiple syllabus mappings.

Example:

```text
TOPIC:
Fundamental Rights

MASTER_SUBJECT:
Polity

MAPPINGS:
- PRELIMS
- GS2
- Ethics
- Social Justice
```

Another:

```text
TOPIC:
Urbanisation

MASTER_SUBJECT:
Society

MAPPINGS:
- GS1
- Sociology Paper II
- Geography
- Economy
- Social Justice
- Environment
```

Another:

```text
TOPIC:
Climate Change

MASTER_SUBJECT:
Environment

MAPPINGS:
- PRELIMS
- GS1 Geography
- GS3 Environment
- Economy
- Disaster Management
- International Relations
- Sociology Paper II
```

This will prevent you from having to mark the same underlying subject matter as "unrevised" five different times.

